      "writtenOn": "2023-07-06T15:39:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Why do we need a string terminator?\n\u003e\n\u003e How does this relate to the previous lines?\n\nTo act as a last-resort `\u0027\\0\u0027` for functions getting C strings from the stack; see [Inseob\u0027s comment](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2399623/comment/ecaaee80_9ed26ab0/) on aosp/2399623 and aosp/2429952.\n\n\u003e Could we just clear the relevant bits in x29 first?\n\nThe `STRB` is a neat way to handle both big- and little-endian at once; see [this comment](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2429952/comments/1b5ece91_a0849b8c) on aosp/2429952.\n\nAnyway, these particular lines will be removed by aosp/2646393; see [Jakob\u0027s comment](https://android-review.git.corp.google.com/c/platform/packages/modules/Virtualization/+/2646393/comment/96f0c41c_5bda5e0a/).",
      "parentUuid": "cce73aea_c6fa98af",
      "range": {
